<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="Foreword.Android.Pages.AwayPage"
             Title="Away">
    <!--
        A1 in the mockups: the pause.

        AWAY IS A DATE RANGE, NOT A MODE. The one thing the owner asked for that Google Tasks cannot
        express. A recurring task that fires while you are away is worse than useless: it prints on a
        page you are not reading and comes back as a backlog you did not fail to do.

        THE IMPORTANT LINE IS THE CAPTION — a paused task is not late and does not pile up. The
        mornings simply pass and the one after is ordinary.

        What is NOT paused matters as much: the morning still goes out, because a holiday is exactly
        when a day sheet earns its place; and anything with a date of its own keeps printing, because
        it did not come from a rule.

        The toggles are the kit's segmented control, not switches (§8), and there is no Save — each
        one commits as it is tapped.

        Mockups: https://claude.ai/code/artifact/6bb65b0d-04da-47f3-bf72-a04020217e0c
    -->
    <ScrollView>
        <VerticalStackLayout Padding="{StaticResource ScreenPadding}" Spacing="0">

            <Label Text="Away" Style="{StaticResource DisplayLabel}" />

            <Label Text="Dates" Style="{StaticResource GroupLabel}" />
            <Border Style="{StaticResource GroupCard}">
                <VerticalStackLayout>
                    <Grid Padding="16,12" ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto">
                        <Label Text="From" Style="{StaticResource CardRowTitle}"
                               VerticalOptions="Center" />
                        <DatePicker Grid.Column="1" x:Name="FromPicker"
                                    DateSelected="OnDatesChanged" />
                    </Grid>
                    <BoxView HeightRequest="1" Color="{StaticResource Hairline}" />
                    <Grid Padding="16,12" ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto">
                        <Label Text="Until" Style="{StaticResource CardRowTitle}"
                               VerticalOptions="Center" />
                        <DatePicker Grid.Column="1" x:Name="UntilPicker"
                                    DateSelected="OnDatesChanged" />
                    </Grid>
                </VerticalStackLayout>
            </Border>
            <Label x:Name="MorningsLabel" Style="{StaticResource CardCaption}" />

            <Label Text="While you are away" Style="{StaticResource GroupLabel}" />
            <Border Style="{StaticResource GroupCard}">
                <VerticalStackLayout x:Name="Toggles" />
            </Border>

            <Label Text="A paused task is not late and does not pile up: the mornings simply pass. Anything with a date of its own still prints."
                   Style="{StaticResource CardCaption}" />

            <Button Text="Not going anywhere" Clicked="OnClearClicked"
                    Style="{StaticResource QuietButton}" HorizontalOptions="Start"
                    Margin="0,24,0,0" />

        </VerticalStackLayout>
    </ScrollView>
</ContentPage>
